        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 64-year-old male, who presented on 17/02/2020 with worsening dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced exercise tolerance consistent with an acute exacerbation of his known COPD. On assessment, oxygen saturation was reduced at 88% on room air. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received thorough patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management. He recovered satisfactorily and was discharged on 18/02/2020 with an oral steroid taper and optimised inhaler regimen. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. I remain available for any queries.</div>"
            },
